# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::CorrPlotPayload`

The numbers behind an autocorrelation plot.

`CorrPlotPayload` is plain data.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lags` | `pluss::Series` | — | The lags plotted, in increasing order. |
| `values` | `pluss::Series` | — | The autocorrelations (or partial autocorrelations) at those lags. |
| `conf_low, conf_high` | `double` | — | The limits `∓z/√n` of the white-noise band. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

